<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · river</p><h1 class="enc-title">Khabur River</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khabur</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Khabur River is a tributary of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/euphrates">Euphrates</a> in north-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/syria">Syria</a>. Its valley was the heartland of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mitanni">Mitanni Empire</a> and its capital <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/washukanni">Washukanni</a>. After the Hittite defeat, Mitanni's remaining territory was confined to the Khabur valley as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hanigalbat">Hanigalbat</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/khabur-river.jpg" alt="Khabur River" width="320" height="214" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Bertramz · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Khabur,SheikhHamad.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
